      "answer": "slope 4, point (−2, 3)",
      "acceptable": [],
      "hints": [
        "Point-slope form is y − y₁ = m(x − x₁).",
        "x + 2 is the same as x − (−2), so x₁ = −2.",
        "y − 3 means y₁ = 3, and m = 4."
      ],
      "solution": "y − 3 = 4(x − (−2)): m = 4, (x₁, y₁) = (−2, 3). Answer: <b>slope 4, point (−2, 3)</b>"
    },
